---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base>
  <!-- ─── Hero ─── -->
  <div class="container">
    <header class="hero">
      <h1 class="hero__headline">I build systems that last.</h1>
      <p class="hero__subtext">
        Not systems that impress at first glance, but systems that remain
        quiet, stable, and correct after the novelty fades. I work where
        data meets uncertainty, and where the real test is not performance
        in isolation, but behavior over time.
      </p>
      <div class="hero__meta">
        <span class="hero__name">Nan Shang, Ph.D.</span>
        <span class="hero__role">Chief Scientist & Founding Engineer</span>
        <span class="hero__org">Drone Institute</span>
      </div>
      <div class="hero__actions">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#overview">Read more</a>
        <a class="btn" href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=TcDAyj0AAAAJ&hl=en"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a>
        <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/leibowivz"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        <a class="btn" href="mailto:nan.shang@droneinstitute.ai">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </header>
  </div>

  <!-- ─── Navigation ─── -->
  <nav class="nav" aria-label="Primary">
    <div class="nav__inner">
      <a class="nav__link" href="#overview">Overview</a>
      <a class="nav__link" href="#approach">Approach</a>
      <a class="nav__link" href="#systems">Systems</a>
      <a class="nav__link" href="#work">Work</a>
      <a class="nav__link" href="#research">Research</a>
      <a class="nav__link" href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <main class="container">

    <!-- ─── Overview ─── -->
    <section id="overview">
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p class="quote-block">
        I design and operate production-grade geospatial and AI systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        My work sits at the intersection of remote sensing research, geospatial
        analytics, and system architecture. I focus on building systems that take
        spatial data — often noisy, incomplete, and operationally constrained — and
        turn it into outputs that can be trusted in real decision-making contexts.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">
        What matters to me is not isolated model performance, but how a system
        behaves end to end: how data enters, how assumptions propagate, how errors
        surface, and how the system evolves under continuous use.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── My Role ─── -->
    <section>
      <h2>My Role</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        As a founding engineer, I designed the core architectures from first
        principles. As chief scientist, I ensure that deployed systems remain
        scientifically grounded as they scale, evolve, and are exposed to real
        operational pressure.
      </p>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li>Define system-level evaluation criteria beyond accuracy alone</li>
        <li>Architect end-to-end geospatial and AI pipelines</li>
        <li>Translate research methods into deployable, auditable systems</li>
        <li>Own trade-offs across accuracy, latency, cost, and reliability</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── Approach ─── -->
    <section id="approach">
      <h2>How I Build Systems</h2>

      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="glass-card">
          <div class="card__num">01</div>
          <div class="card__title">Production is the benchmark</div>
          <p class="card__text">
            A system is only meaningful if it continues to behave correctly
            after deployment. I design systems to fail visibly rather than
            silently, to support iteration without destabilization, and to
            remain interpretable to engineers and operators.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="glass-card">
          <div class="card__num">02</div>
          <div class="card__title">Constraints shape architecture</div>
          <p class="card__text">
            Latency, throughput, cost envelopes, and operational friction are
            architectural facts. I treat these constraints as inputs to design
            decisions, making trade-offs explicit so systems can be reasoned
            about and maintained over time.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="glass-card">
          <div class="card__num">03</div>
          <div class="card__title">Deployment reveals assumptions</div>
          <p class="card__text">
            Research does not end at deployment. I design feedback loops that
            surface failure modes, quantify drift, and allow systems to improve
            without eroding trust or stability.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="glass-card">
          <div class="card__num">04</div>
          <div class="card__title">Data quality compounds</div>
          <p class="card__text">
            Long-term system advantage comes from disciplined data practices.
            I build pipelines where ingestion, annotation, quality control,
            monitoring, retraining, and rollback strategies reinforce one another.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── Systems I Build ─── -->
    <section id="systems">
      <h2>Systems I Build</h2>

      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="glass-card">
          <div class="card__label">Pipelines</div>
          <div class="card__title">End-to-End Geospatial</div>
          <p class="card__text">
            Pipelines covering the full lifecycle of spatial data — from
            ingestion and normalization to processing, verification, reporting,
            and delivery. Designed to be repeatable, auditable, and resilient
            under scale.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="glass-card">
          <div class="card__label">Sensing</div>
          <div class="card__title">Multimodal Remote Sensing</div>
          <p class="card__text">
            Workflows across RGB imagery, thermal and infrared data, and
            derived spatial layers. Focus on extracting actionable signals
            while controlling uncertainty and false positives in operational
            environments.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="glass-card">
          <div class="card__label">Quality</div>
          <div class="card__title">Verification & QC</div>
          <p class="card__text">
            Spatial systems often fail quietly through projection errors,
            unit mismatches, alignment drift, or metadata assumptions.
            Verification layers — automated and human-in-the-loop — that
            make failures observable and traceable.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="glass-card">
          <div class="card__label">Delivery</div>
          <div class="card__title">Secure Data Delivery</div>
          <p class="card__text">
            Delivery systems with clear permission boundaries, multi-tenant
            access control, lifecycle management, and audit-friendly
            access patterns.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── Selected Work ─── -->
    <section id="work">
      <h2>Selected Work</h2>
      <blockquote>
        Public descriptions focus on architectural patterns and operational
        behavior, not on clients, locations, or proprietary metrics.
      </blockquote>

      <div class="grid-1">
        <div class="glass-card">
          <h3>Production Geospatial Intelligence Platforms</h3>
          <p class="card__text" style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
            Large-scale geospatial processing platforms built to support
            continuous operation, repeatable results, and controlled iteration
            under real-world constraints.
          </p>
          <ul class="feature-list">
            <li>Ingest high-volume spatial data from heterogeneous sources</li>
            <li>Normalize and align data across coordinate systems and resolutions</li>
            <li>Execute analytics and inference at scale</li>
            <li>Embed verification and QC as part of the execution path</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="glass-card">
          <h3>Multisensor Analysis and Decision Pipelines</h3>
          <p class="card__text" style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
            Pipelines that combine RGB imagery, thermal and infrared signals,
            and derived spatial features. Emphasis on extracting decision-relevant
            signals and minimizing false positives where ground truth is incomplete.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="glass-card">
          <h3>Verification-Centric System Design</h3>
          <ul class="feature-list">
            <li>Surface spatial inconsistencies — alignment, scale, unit errors</li>
            <li>Detect silent failure modes before downstream impact</li>
            <li>Integrate automated checks with human-in-the-loop review</li>
            <li>Verification artifacts treated as first-class outputs</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="grid-2">
          <div class="glass-card">
            <h3>Data-Centric AI Production Loops</h3>
            <ul class="feature-list">
              <li>Continuously measured and corrected data quality</li>
              <li>Structured annotation and re-annotation pipelines</li>
              <li>Retraining driven by observed failure modes</li>
              <li>Rollback and comparison as operational controls</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="glass-card">
            <h3>Secure Multi-Tenant Delivery</h3>
            <ul class="feature-list">
              <li>Strict tenant isolation</li>
              <li>Granular access control</li>
              <li>Data lifecycle and retention management</li>
              <li>Audit-friendly access patterns</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── Research ─── -->
    <section id="research">
      <h2>Research & Its Connection to Production</h2>
      <p>
        My research background is in remote sensing and geospatial analysis,
        and it directly informs the systems I build today. My peer-reviewed
        work addresses questions that recur in production systems:
      </p>
      <ul class="feature-list" style="margin-top: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
        <li>How spatial measurements behave under noise and scale</li>
        <li>How resolution, alignment, and representation affect downstream inference</li>
        <li>How to reason about uncertainty in derived spatial products</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These research insights shape practical decisions in system design,
        including data preprocessing, model selection, validation strategies,
        and quality control thresholds.
      </p>

      <div style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <div class="kv-item__key" style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 0.65rem;">Domains</div>
        <ul class="tags">
          <li>GIS & Spatial Analytics</li>
          <li>LiDAR & 3D Processing</li>
          <li>Remote Sensing</li>
          <li>Geospatial AI</li>
          <li>Production ML Systems</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="link-row" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=TcDAyj0AAAAJ&hl=en"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── Writing ─── -->
    <section>
      <h2>Writing</h2>
      <p>
        Technical notes on production AI systems, geospatial data failure modes,
        and system-level decision-making under constraints. Focused on what holds,
        what fails, and how to design systems that remain reliable as they evolve.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── Contact ─── -->
    <section id="contact">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <ul class="contact-list">
        <li><a href="mailto:nan.shang@droneinstitute.ai">nan.shang@droneinstitute.ai</a></li>
        <li><a href="mailto:sn1514826@gmail.com">sn1514826@gmail.com</a></li>
      </ul>
      <div class="link-row">
        <a href="https://github.com/leibowivz" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=TcDAyj0AAAAJ&hl=en"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <footer>
      <p>Nan Shang, Ph.D.</p>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Base>
